  STEP 3 — tools/call get_tdd_state (where are we?)
========================================================================
JSON-RPC request: method="tools/call" params={"name":"get_tdd_state","arguments":{}}
Result:
    {
      "instructions": "This file is the TDD phase log. `instructions` is this guide, not workflow state. `entries` is chronological, oldest first; each entry is the machine at `timestamp` (UTC RFC 3339). `phase` is START, RED, GREEN, or REFACTOR. Never refactor on RED; never mark a requirement implemented off GREEN. `lastRun` is test counts at that moment; failure details live on the test-run reply. `refactorLog` is every bdd refactor --note, in order. `attemptLog` is model implementation attempts for the requirement in flight; a GREEN run clears it. Each attempt records what it wrote (`targets`), the failures it was briefed with (`failures`), and the output of the first run after it (`outcome`; empty means no run verified it). When briefing a model, include only the three most recent entries. Older entries stay on disk for humans.",
